	(text "SENSOR SUPPLY (section 13.5). One 5V terminal for flow meters with electronics, fed from V_BUCK:\noff on USB power. GPIO45 (SENS_PWR_EN, a strapping pin held low by R86) turns it on.\nU11 TPS2553 with R83 = 200k limits at 135 mA (116 to 158 mA) and reports on SENS_FLT_N.\nTerminal voltage about 4.8 V at 20 mA, 4.5 V at 50 mA. Treat 100 mA as the usable current.\nD19 blocks a +45 V miswire. D20 clamps a negative one and F3 (0.2 A hold) trips.\nD24 keeps the OUT pin of U11 above -0.3 V while F3 is tripping."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 248.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bd887cfa-ca6f-57a0-b110-ce8d5181fed4")
	)
	(text "SENSOR INPUTS (hardware design section 13).\n\nEach terminal has a 10k pull-up to V5 (0.5 mA wetting\ncurrent), 10k in series, a BAT54S clamp to 3V3 and GND,\n22 nF and 1k into the GPIO. A closed contact or an\nopen-collector sensor reads low. The filter passes 200 Hz.\nIt does not remove the 1 to 2 ms bounce of a reed-switch\nmeter; firmware does.\n\n32 VAC on a signal terminal for ever is survived: the TVS\ndoes not conduct below 48 V, and the pull-up and series\nresistors are 1206 parts rated 200 V that dissipate 0.11 W.\nThe clamp passes 4.2 mA peak into 3V3.\n\nD12, D13, D14, D18: SMBJ48CA at each field terminal,\nclamping at 77.4 V. Place each at its terminal, with a PCB\nspark gap where the layout allows.\n\nThe GND terminals of J4 are circuit ground, which is the\ntransformer leg AC_N."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 198.12 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cbfd1b3b-63ec-5b29-9344-67c485f22876")
	)
